<title>SOUTH KOREA: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>SOUTH KOREA GOVERNMENT LIST (970806)</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p> * 18 Dec 97 - Presidential Elections				*</p>
<p> *************************************************************</p>
<p>  President........KIM Young-sam</p>
<p>(sworn in 25 Feb 93 for a five-year term)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Formed 26 February 93, latest reshuffle 5 Aug 97)</p>
<p>  Prime Minister (appointed March 4, 1997).............KOH Kun</p>
<p>Deputy Prime Minister, Finance &amp; Economy.....KANG Kyong-shik</p>
<p>  Deputy Prime Minister, National Unification.......KWON O-kie</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p>  Agriculture &amp; Forestry............LEE Hyo-gae</p>
<p>  Construction &amp; Transportation...LEE Hwan-kyun   Culture &amp; Sports...SONG Tae-ho</p>
<p>  Education.......LEE Myung-hyun</p>
<p>  Environment......YOON Yeo-joon</p>
<p>  Finance &amp; Economy...See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p>  Foreign Affairs...YOO Chong-ha</p>
<p>  Government Administration......SHIM Woo-young</p>
<p>  Health &amp; Welfare....CHOI Kwang</p>
<p>  Home Affairs....CHO Hae-nyoung</p>
<p>  Information.........OH In-whan</p>
<p>  Information &amp; Communication....KANG Bong-gyun</p>
<p>  Justice...........KIM Jong-koo</p>
<p>  Labour...............LEE Ki-ho</p>
<p>Maritime Affairs..JOH Jung-jay</p>
<p>National Defence..KIM Dong-jin</p>
<p>  National Unification...............See Deputy Prime Minister</p>
<p>  Political Affairs (First).........HONG Sa-duk</p>
<p>  Political Affairs (Second).......LEE Yun-sook</p>
<p>  Science &amp; Technology.............KWUN Sook-il</p>
<p>  Trade, Industry &amp; Energy.......LIM Chang-yeul</p>
<p>				_ _ _ _ _ _ _</p>
<p>Other important office holders:</p>
<p>Director of the Agency for</p>
<p>National Security Planning..KWON Young-hae</p>
<p>  Legislation Minister............SONG Jong-eui</p>
<p>  Patriots &amp; Veterans Affairs Minister.......... PARK Sang-bum</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>  Parliament Speaker................KIM Soo-han</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
<p>Governor of the Bank of Korea.LEE Kyung-shick</p>
<p>				- - - - - - -</p>
